# Line endings, pinned so that a checkout cannot break the things that run.
#
# Git's autocrlf would otherwise hand a Windows checkout CRLF, and `make e2e` runs
# `sh scripts/e2e.sh` — which fails on the carriage returns before it runs a single
# check. The same applies to anything else a shell or a container reads.
#
# Normalising to LF in the working tree on every platform is the boring choice that
# keeps one file usable everywhere: Python does not care either way, and nothing
# here needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Genuinely binary, and must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gguf binary
*.safetensors binary
